.TH "BINDLE_URLDESC" "3" "@RELEASE_MONTH@" "@PACKAGE_NAME@" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
bindle_hash_set, bindle_hash_sset, bindle_hash_set_str, bindle_hash_sset_str - Bindle Binary Tools hash table set routines

.SH LIBRARY
Bindle Binaries Tools (libbindle, -lbindle)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include\fR \fB<bindle.h>\fR
.sp
.BI "int bindle_hash_set( bindle_hash_t * " bh ", const void * " key ,
.BI "                     size_t " key_len ", const void * " val ,
.BI "                     size_t " val_len " );"
.sp
.BI "int bindle_hash_set_str( bindle_hash_t * " bh ", const void * " key ,
.BI "                         size_t " key_len ", const char * " val " );"
.sp
.BI "int bindle_hash_sset( bindle_hash_t * " bh ", const char * " key ,
.BI "                      const void * " val ", size_t " val_len " );"
.sp
.BI "int bindle_hash_sset_str( bindle_hash_t * " bh ", const char * " key ,
.BI "                          const char * " val " );"
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBbindle_hash_set\fR() function modifies the hash table refernced by
\fIbh\fR by setting the value for the binary key referenced by \fIkey\fR of
\fIkey_len\fR bytes length.  The value is referenced by \fIval\fR of
\fIval_len\fR bytes length.
.sp
The \fBbindle_hash_set_str\fR() function is a wrapper for
\fBbindle_hash_set\fR(). \fBbindle_hash_set_str\fR() is the equivalent of
.RS 6
.TP 15 
.BI "bindle_hash_set( " bh ", " key ", " key_len ", " val ", strlen( " val " )+1 )"
.RE
.PP
.sp
The \fBbindle_hash_sset\fR() function is a wrapper for
\fBbindle_hash_set\fR(). \fBbindle_hash_sset\fR() is the equivalent of
.RS 6
.TP 15 
.BI "bindle_hash_set( " bh ", " key ", strlen( " key " )+1, " val ", " val_len " )"
.RE
.PP
.sp
The \fBbindle_hash_sset_str\fR() function is a wrapper for
\fBbindle_hash_set\fR(). \fBbindle_hash_sset_str\fR() is the equivalent of
.RS 6
.TP 15 
.BI "bindle_hash_set( " bh ", " key ", strlen( " key " )+1, " val ", strlen( " val " )+1 )"
.RE
.PP

.SH RETURN VALUES
The \fBbindle_hash_set\fR(), \fBbindle_hash_set_str\fR,
\fBbindle_hash_sset\fR, and \fBbindle_hash_sset_str\fR functions return 0
if successful. If an error was encountered, \fIerrno\fR will be set and the
functions will return -1.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bindletools (3),
.BR bindle_hash_initialize (3),
.BR bindle_hash_del (3),
.BR bindle_hash_get (3),
.BR bindle_hash_keys (3),
.BR bindle_hash_funcs (3)

